{{Navbar-Global Gas Infrastructure Tracker}}
'''Houston Gas Pipeline (HPL) System''' is a natural gas pipeline.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|url=https://hpletconnect.energytransfer.com/ipost/HPL/capacity/design-capacity-for-intrastates|title=Energy Transfer|website=hpletconnect.energytransfer.com|language=en|access-date=2023-08-24}}</ref>

==Location==
HPL is an intrastate pipeline system in eastern Texas and the western Gulf of Mexico. It has multiple start and end points.

{{#display_map:
|lines=33.632786, -96.772354:32.472563, -95.344132:29.859566, -95.344132:27.790358, -97.442526:26.943988, -98.285743;27.790358, -97.442526:29.394019, -98.582368;29.394019, -98.582368:29.754904, -95.362889;29.394019, -98.582368:27.800280, -99.460794;29.394019, -98.582368:30.295604, -97.747957;29.859566, -95.344132:30.532471, -96.023109:30.295604, -97.747957|center=29.859566, -95.344132|width=400|height=300|type=normal|zoom=5}}

==Project Details==
*'''Operator: '''Energy Transfer Partners
*'''Owner:''' Energy Transfer Partners
*'''Current capacity:''' 5300 Million cubic feet per day<ref name=":0" />
*'''Length: ''' 3800 miles /  6116 km<ref name=":0" />
*'''Status: '''Operating
*'''Start Year: '''

==Background==
The HPL System is an extensive network of intrastate natural gas pipelines, an underground Bammel storage reservoir, and related transportation assets. The system has access to multiple sources of historically significant natural gas supply reserves from South Texas, the Gulf Coast of Texas, East Texas and the western Gulf of Mexico, and is directly connected to major gas distribution, electric and industrial load centers in Houston, Corpus Christi, Texas City and other cities located along the Gulf Coast of Texas.<ref name=":0" />

In 2001, AEP Energy Services Gas Holding Co., a subsidiary of American Electric Power Company acquired Houston Gas Pipeline from Enron Corp.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.electricnet.com/doc/aep-will-buy-enrons-houston-pipeline-company-0001|title=AEP will buy Enron's Houston Pipeline Company|website=www.electricnet.com|access-date=2023-08-24}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.power-eng.com/news/aep-completes-purchase-of-houston-pipe-line-company-from-enron/#gref|title=AEP completes purchase of Houston Pipe Line Company from Enron|last=Clarion Energy Content Directors|date=2001-06-05|work=Power Engineering|access-date=2023-08-24|language=en-US}}</ref> In January 2005 Energy Transfer Partners announced the acquisition of Houston Pipeline from American Electric Power Company.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1012569/000119312505053153/d8ka.htm|title=Energy Transfer Partners, LP: Current Report|last=|first=|date=17 March, 2005|website=U.S. Securities & Exchange Commission|url-status=live|archive-url=|archive-date=|access-date=25 August, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.energyintel.com/0000017b-a7a6-de4c-a17b-e7e6adac0001|title=Energy Transfer Partners Adds Houston Pipe Line to Holdings|date=2005-01-28|work=Energy Intelligence|access-date=2023-08-24|language=en}}</ref>

